<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#black-ships">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Ships</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1853">1853</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Ships was the Japanese name for the Western vessels, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steamship">steam-powered warships</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry">Commodore Matthew Perry</a>'s American squadron that entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-bay">Edo Bay</a> in 1853. Perry demanded the opening of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> to American commerce. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>'s inability to resist or accommodate the demand exposed the military weakness of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>.</p></div>
